Useful and important K8 commands

kubectl config view - provides cluster, context details 

kubectl config current-context - provides details of the current context

kubectl config use-context "context name" : to swtich between context 

aws eks update-kubeconfig --region "region name" --name "name of the cluster" - adding cluster to kubeconfig file

kubectl apply -f serviceaccount.yml - to create custom service account

kubectl get sa - to get the list of sa accounts 

kubectl apply -f complete-deploy.yml - to deply the app in k8
